     "extraction_status": "extracted",
     "value": "Participants were instructed to view each series of photographs and to try to remember them for a recognition test upon completion of the scanning session. Subjects were not informed of the food-related content of the photographs.",
     "value_source": "reported"
    },
    "stimuli": {
     "extraction_status": "extracted",
     "value": "Professional quality full-color photographs obtained from commercial stock photography Web sites. Low-calorie photographs depicted freshly prepared garden salads, whole-grain cereals, fresh vegetables, and fruits; high-calorie photographs included french fries, ice cream sundaes, cheeseburgers, hot dogs, chocolate chip cookies, barbequed chicken, strawberry shortcake, and pasta with meat sauce; utensil photographs depicted forks, spoons, dishes, placemats, chopsticks, and tableware, with no edible items present. Control block images consisted of photographs of visually interesting objects generally not consumed as food in modern western cultures, such as rocks, shrubs, bricks, trees, and flowers.",
     "value_source": "reported"
